{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world","id":974902,"title":"How 'aware' is The World?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-22T23:07:46-07:00","id":974902,"title":"How 'aware' is The World?","content":"Of all the fun things in Scion 2e, the one I'm most excited for is more information on the actual setting this time around. Neall has previously said that there's no 'Masquerade' to speak of, but I have to wonder what the average mortal knows about. Polytheism has survived in a big way compared to our reality, but would Zeus showing up and announcing himself be something plausible or would it be as believable to someone of The World as the average 'second coming of Christ' is to one of us? Are say, satyrs or naga out there living in their own little known communities, or do nutjobs in tinfoil hats spread blurry footage of valkyries instead of aliens? Is a Scion throwing fire from her fingertips extraordinary but possible, or would people view that as an impossible, crazy thing?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T23:28:29-07:00","id":974906,"title":"","content":"Gods play it careful with direct revelation to the mortal world because that invites Fatebinding (which is much more powerful on their level than for Origin/Hero level Scions). So there should be room for atheists or monotheists to exist in the World without that person needing to delusionally deny the blatantly obvious (at least for npcs... pcs are going to be faced with divinities and their world-view will need to account for them).<br /> <br /> I am really curious too about the degree to which the nonhuman races like Alfar, Satyrs, Naga, etc actively conceal their existence or not, and if they do, why do they (since they don't have to worry about Fatebinding from &quot;revelation&quot; the way gods do).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T23:36:48-07:00","id":974907,"title":"","content":"I imagine that there's no Masquerade in the sense of most supernatural beings are deliberately taking actions to keep humans unaware.<br /> <br /> If there IS one, it probably lies in humans' ability to put blinders on. That's not a dwarf, that's a little person. That elf? Just a VERY pretty Swedish man.<br /> <br /> That's not a dryad, that's a nudist farmer who REALLY needs to find Jesus and learn to throw a robe on when the mailman visits. (The &quot;Dryad who needs to find Jesus&quot; courtesy of a PC in the group I'm part of)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T00:01:32-07:00","id":974917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=974906#post974906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am really curious too about the degree to which the nonhuman races like Alfar, Satyrs, Naga, etc actively conceal their existence or not, and if they do, why do they (since they don't have to worry about Fatebinding from &quot;revelation&quot; the way gods do).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-world-scion-second-edition-open-development/\" target=\"_blank\">Quoth Neall:</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the cracks of the World are Creatures of Legend, sitting ever within humanity\u2019s collective peripheral vision. They hide in plain sight, when they bother to hide at all. Dwarves and elves are in towns in the Scandinavian countries, sometimes even plying their trade. Centaurs herd in the plains of Thessaly, where there are so few cameras. Tengu nests nestle among Japanese skyscrapers. Colonies of satyrs in the mountains of Greece, fighting for territory with the aforementioned centaurs who lope across the plains. In the American West, a different kind of centaur rides the highways on two wheels, chrome where human legs should be and oil pumping in their hearts. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T00:10:32-07:00","id":974921,"title":"","content":"*deleting angry ranting about urban fantasy setting getting human nature backwards*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:06:35-07:00","id":974945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=974921#post974921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*deleting angry ranting about urban fantasy setting getting human nature backwards*</div> </div> </div> </div>Now you have me intrigued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:14:14-07:00","id":974947,"title":"","content":"The existence of real magical creatures isn't enough to stop conspiracy theorists from obsessing over fake ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T02:18:50-07:00","id":974949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=974947#post974947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The existence of real magical creatures isn't enough to stop conspiracy theorists from obsessing over fake ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>If anything it'll lead to even crazier fake ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T12:47:19-07:00","id":975176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vonpenguin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=974949#post974949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If anything it'll lead to even crazier fake ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Psh, forget those doctored pictures of pixies. I've got REAL evidence that the President and the British Prime Minister are <i>reptilians</i> wearing human skinsuits!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:05:17-07:00","id":975186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=974945#post974945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Now you have me intrigued.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the idea that humanity as a group will stubbornly refuse to believe in magic that is in front of their face to cling to the idea of a safer more predictable world, is the opposite of how collective human nature works.<br /> <br /> Humans as groups are paranoid, not stubbornly skeptical trying to believe they're safer than they are.<br /> <br /> Furthermore belief in the supernatural only historically declined at all in response to empiricism debunking it. In a world where the supernatural was real, empiricism and the enlightenment wouldn't have produced those results in the first place. Science and the &quot;supernatural&quot; are only at odds in our consciousness because we live in a world where the former debunks the latter. If the latter existed the former would reveal it, not debunk it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:13:17-07:00","id":975190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975186#post975186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the latter existed the former would reveal it, not debunk it.</div> </div> </div> </div>We live in a world where many people believe, despite literally all the evidence debunking it, that vaccines cause autism. (And that is the last I will get into that because thinking on that topic makes me see red and I just start shrieking like a mandrake)<br /> <br /> Humans can be <i>very</i> clingy with their worldviews.<br /> <br /> Edit: I mean I won't say you're wrong, that's a very valid mindset. I'm just saying that people <i>are</i> very capable of cherry-picking things that support their preconceptions and bias while dismissing things that fly in the face of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 09-23-2016, 04:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:14:58-07:00","id":975192,"title":"","content":"Thanks, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a>. I appreciate the answer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:21:29-07:00","id":975200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975190#post975190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We live in a world where many people believe, despite literally all the evidence debunking it, that vaccines cause autism. (And that is the last I will get into that because thinking on that topic makes me see red and I just start shrieking like a mandrake)<br /> <br /> Humans can be <i>very</i> clingy with their worldviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>that was the point of the first part of my post. Humans are paranoid and superstitious.<br /> <br /> Refusing to believe in a world of magic that empirically DOES exist isn't that. The idea that it didn't exist would never even have arisen in the first place since empiricism would be on he side that it does, so where would the anti-supernatural arguments have even arisen from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T13:25:23-07:00","id":975202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975200#post975200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Refusing to believe in a world of magic that empirically DOES exist isn't that. The idea that it didn't exist would never even have arisen in the first place since empiricism would be on he side that it does, so where would the anti-supernatural arguments have even arisen from?</div> </div> </div> </div>That, I honestly don't have an answer for. I guess I was more thinking of your post saying that it &quot;tends to ignore human nature&quot;, which stuck with me because no, clinging to an incorrect worldview in spite of overwhelming evidence is <i>very</i> human.<br /> <br /> Guess we'll have to see if there's a reason for it in the Origins book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T15:04:55-07:00","id":975246,"title":"","content":"My reading is that it isn't so much humans refuse to accept supernatural events, but rather they do exist, and have existed so long no one cares. They exist either intermingled like some dwarves and Alfar or they prefer places where they won't be bothered.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8375-vonpenguin","name":"vonpenguin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T15:11:03-07:00","id":975248,"title":"","content":"I'd be cool with an explanation that humans have a history of killing dwarves/naga/vanara/satyrs/nunnehi/tengu/etc and taking their stuff, so those communities tend to avoid humans and take advantage of Terra Incognita where they can.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T01:19:03-07:00","id":975420,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, Gods in Scion 2e won't be affected by humanity's preconceived ideas of who and what they are. If that is the case, I imagine they would be able to operate a lot more openly with them, though still may get affected by Fatebinding if they're not careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T01:26:17-07:00","id":975423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975186#post975186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically the idea that humanity as a group will stubbornly refuse to believe in magic that is in front of their face to cling to the idea of a safer more predictable world, is the opposite of how collective human nature works.<br /> <br /> Humans as groups are paranoid, not stubbornly skeptical trying to believe they're safer than they are.<br /> <br /> Furthermore belief in the supernatural only historically declined at all in response to empiricism debunking it. In a world where the supernatural was real, empiricism and the enlightenment wouldn't have produced those results in the first place. Science and the &quot;supernatural&quot; are only at odds in our consciousness because we live in a world where the former debunks the latter. If the latter existed the former would reveal it, not debunk it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. If somebody came up to me on the street and started performing real miracles / magic in front of my eyes and could prove it was supernatural in origin, I admit I would be shocked at first. But after that wore off, I'd probably chase them across the city <i>demanding to learn more!</i><br /> <br /> Humanity doesn't believe in the supernatural because we've reached a point where we can disprove what we once considered to be supernatural. That's not the same thing as saying we're mentally incapable of acknowledging it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for humans that deny empirical evidence, most of the those cases relate to people who have been indoctrinated into their beliefs. They've had their ideas drilled into them over a long period of time and the idea of abandoning them in scary. But if you take the same ideas and show them to somebody who hasn't gone through the process of indoctrination, they're more inclined to see things from an educated point of view, and thus would be more willing to believe the evidence presented before them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-24-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T02:34:58-07:00","id":975439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975420#post975420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, Gods in Scion 2e won't be affected by humanity's preconceived ideas of who and what they are. If that is the case, I imagine they would be able to operate a lot more openly with them, though still may get affected by Fatebinding if they're not careful.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm sorry, but... what?<br /> <br /> How can they not be affected by human's ideas of who and what they are, but still have to worry about Fatebindings? They're the same thing, aren't they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12300,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","user":"Crying","date":". 09-25-2016, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T02:50:33-07:00","id":975444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975439#post975439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm sorry, but... what?<br /> <br /> How can they not be affected by human's idead of who and what they are, but still have to worry about Fatebindings? They're the same thing, aren't they?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I admit, I'm curious about that, too. But I asked this question a while ago on these forums and got a reply saying that the belief of mortals will not have an impact on what the Gods become.<br /> <br /> <b>My best guess?</b><br /> <br /> Fatebinding is going to be tweaked so that it now relates to how your Scion is already behaving, instead of deciding their future for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T03:10:07-07:00","id":975452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975444#post975444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I admit, I'm curious about that, too. But I asked this question a while ago on these forums and got a reply saying that the belief of mortals will not have an impact on what the Gods become.<br /> <br /> <b>My best guess?</b><br /> <br /> Fatebinding is going to be tweaked so that it now relates to how your Scion is already behaving, instead of deciding their future for them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That... sounds kind of dumb. I might end up using the old Fatebinding system if that's true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12300-crying","name":"Crying","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12300_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T08:39:05-07:00","id":975534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crying</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975452#post975452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That... sounds kind of dumb. I might end up using the old Fatebinding system if that's true.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I said, it was only <i>my personal guess</i>. It's not like I'm one of the developers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But I like that idea better, in my opinion. It makes more sense for a Companion, or a Rival to be created through personal experience. Spending time with that person and strengthening your bond. Instead of Fate just suddenly dropping a stranger in your lap and saying <i>&quot;you love / hate each other now!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T09:25:54-07:00","id":975553,"title":"","content":"I've read that they are making an effort to support both styles (and I think 2 others as well)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T10:39:04-07:00","id":975585,"title":"","content":"That's how it works for hero level scions, Fate's a cheerleader, at demigod, when your legend starts crystalize then the cheerleader pulls a knife and goes all Cathy Bates on you. by the time your a god, Fates' holding you and your family hostage and whispering commands in your ear based on what people expect of you. that's why gods Incarnate as legend 1 mortals, so they have a chance to make the cheerleader calm down and loosen up... unfortunately, a lot of what Fate did had more to do with your personality than the gods might want to admit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-24T23:59:16-07:00","id":975859,"title":"","content":"I suspect it'll be very hard for me to not run a version of the World where there are campaigns to save the Nixies, Frank in accounting is a Sasquach, and people turning into foxes or vice versa is just a thing. I might well borrow heavily from the Incryptid series, save that everyone knows about the various subcultures, if they care to anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T07:35:04-07:00","id":975939,"title":"","content":"One possible example how it may work in fiction is &quot;The Wicked + The Divine&quot;, which Neall has stated is a very direct inspiration for the 'no masquerade' model of play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12349-evilnerf","name":"evilnerf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12349_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T13:57:31-07:00","id":976081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evilnerf</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=975939#post975939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One possible example how it may work in fiction is &quot;The Wicked + The Divine&quot;, which Neall has stated is a very direct inspiration for the 'no masquerade' model of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although W+D is a somewhat more nuanced example of &quot;no masquerade&quot; than it might seem. The recurrence of the Gods is a known historical fact, but there's so little evidence than Cassandra could reasonably think the whole thing was a sham\u2014until Luci went big in public.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:04:55-07:00","id":976113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=976081#post976081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although W+D is a somewhat more nuanced example of &quot;no masquerade&quot; than it might seem. The recurrence of the Gods is a known historical fact, but there's so little evidence than Cassandra could reasonably think the whole thing was a sham\u2014until Luci went big in public.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what I'm getting from this is:<br /> <br /> The Gods used to act a lot more openly back in the old days, but Fate smacked them around a bit and they generally retired from the limelight, working through intermediaries. The monsters went to sleep in their lairs and prisons, and the magical folk kept to themselves, interacting with a very few they knew they could trust.<br /> <br /> By the time the Enlightenment and the scientific method rolled around, evidence of the supernatural was so rare and inconclusive that science took the most rational explanation and people went on with their lives much as they did in our world. Sometimes the mystical and the mundane intertwined, but it was so infrequent the stories slipped through the cracks as fairy tales.<br /> <br /> And now that the Titans are breaking free from their prisons, centaurs of metal terrorize the highways, the sun sometimes runs backwards, and trolls have been sighted coming down from the forests and mountains.<br /> <br /> What masquerade there was was weak to begin with, and now all of mythology is about to come crashing back into mortal life.<br /> <br /> ... That's not accurate at all, is it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:10:29-07:00","id":976114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=976113#post976113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what I'm getting from this is:<br /> <br /> The Gods used to act a lot more openly back in the old days, but Fate smacked them around a bit and they generally retired from the limelight, working through intermediaries. The monsters went to sleep in their lairs and prisons, and the magical folk kept to themselves, interacting with a very few they knew they could trust.<br /> <br /> By the time the Enlightenment and the scientific method rolled around, evidence of the supernatural was so rare and inconclusive that science took the most rational explanation and people went on with their lives much as they did in our world. Sometimes the mystical and the mundane intertwined, but it was so infrequent the stories slipped through the cracks as fairy tales.<br /> <br /> And now that the Titans are breaking free from their prisons, centaurs of metal terrorize the highways, the sun sometimes runs backwards, and trolls have been sighted coming down from the forests and mountains.<br /> <br /> What masquerade there was was weak to begin with, and now all of mythology is about to come crashing back into mortal life.<br /> <br /> ... That's not accurate at all, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a fun Shard.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:14:13-07:00","id":976116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=976113#post976113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... That's not accurate at all, is it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, it's not.<br /> <br /> A monotheist who believes that their God is the true one, and that all the others are either unworthy of worship or not &quot;real&quot; Gods isn't being unreasonable. An atheist who decides that the so-called &quot;Gods&quot; are really just extradimensional aliens using masks drawn from human history to deceive us and that Scions are half-alien hybrids isn't necessarily unreasonable. All myths are true, but most people don't know all of the myths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:22:17-07:00","id":976119,"title":"","content":"I suppose part of it, at least for me, is how common are Scions? Since at least those at the Hero-level seem to be able to act more in the open, what is stopping the social Scions from essentially running entire countries or crafting Scions from sending humanity into a shining future? Is it a sort of Mutually Assured Destruction thing where the threat of opposing Scions prevents too overt of action, or somrthing else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1897-ffanxii4ever","name":"ffanxii4ever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1897_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T15:24:51-07:00","id":976120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=976116#post976116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An atheist who decides that the so-called &quot;Gods&quot; are really just extradimensional aliens using masks drawn from human history to deceive us and that Scions are half-alien hybrids isn't necessarily unreasonable</div> </div> </div> </div>So Stargate SG-1 fans have some vindication? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:00:29-07:00","id":976134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=976116#post976116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, it's not.<br /> <br /> A monotheist who believes that their God is the true one, and that all the others are either unworthy of worship or not &quot;real&quot; Gods isn't being unreasonable. An atheist who decides that the so-called &quot;Gods&quot; are really just extradimensional aliens using masks drawn from human history to deceive us and that Scions are half-alien hybrids isn't necessarily unreasonable. All myths are true, but most people don't know all of the myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>... This is confusing as hell.<br /> <br /> I'll just be quiet and wait for what the book says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T16:28:13-07:00","id":976156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ffanxii4ever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=976119#post976119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose part of it, at least for me, is how common are Scions? Since at least those at the Hero-level seem to be able to act more in the open, what is stopping the social Scions from essentially running entire countries or crafting Scions from sending humanity into a shining future? Is it a sort of Mutually Assured Destruction thing where the threat of opposing Scions prevents too overt of action, or somrthing else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neall has said that the thing about taking over a country is.... Great! You're now the god-king (or god-president) or whatever! Good job.<br /> <br /> Now you actually have to <i>run the country</i>.<br /> <br /> Good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/103-gsd","name":"GSD","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:36:58-07:00","id":976267,"title":"","content":"*Reads latest KS Update*<br /> <br /> Okay, so stuff like &quot;how much the World's mortals actually know&quot; and other setting details is customizable to taste. Okay.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm feeling bluuuueeeee~","edited":{"userid":175,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","user":"Prometheus878","date":". 09-25-2016, 10:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175-prometheus878","name":"Prometheus878","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar175_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:52:29-07:00","id":976283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheus878</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/974902-how-aware-is-the-world?p=976267#post976267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Reads latest KS Update*<br /> <br /> Okay, so stuff like &quot;how much the World's mortals actually know&quot; and other setting details is customizable to taste. Okay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that we've been given mechanical dials in the form of the Modes of Play, I'm not terribly surprised to see them in the lore as well. Modularity is a big push in games these days and I'm glad to see it.<br /> <br /> And now I'm wondering if there will be outright Shards in the book somewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T19:53:40-07:00","id":976284,"title":"","content":"From the Kickstarter update:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neall:<br /> In Second Edition, we're expanding Scion's setting in terms of both scope and verisimilitude, while also emphasizing playability. We present a default setting that has gods moving behind the events of much of history (who\u2019s to say they didn\u2019t?) and prime ministers half-heartedly denying the existence of troll preserves, and we also present a lot of options for the Storyguide to perfectly tailor the sentiment and revelations of the World to their players. Scion can be presented many ways.<br /> Here are some snippets from our setting chapter by Meghan Fitzgerald:<br /> ---<br /> Four and a half billion years ago, a ball of molten dust and raw, sun-forged elements coalesced into a planet. Yet the World is Tiamat, carved into shape and form by Marduk. It is Rangi and Papi, locked in their embrace while their children war within them. It was created by a wagtail swimming upon an infinite ocean, and by Q\u2019uq\u2019umatz and Tepeu speaking the word \u201cearth\u201d when floating upon a similar infinite ocean. Atum existed within a very similar ocean, containing all the World within himself, taking the definitions and limits of existence from the Primordial Deities and granting stewardship to the Ennead until he was named. The sons of Burr lifted the World out of another infinite sea, fashioned from the bones and flesh and maggots of long-dead Ymir.<br /> <br /> For explorers of the World's vast reaches, its layers upon layers of paradoxical mythology and cycles of death and rebirth provide endless fragments of half-real places, things that both do and do not exist at once. Echoes of humanity's first flame burn in dozens of forgotten niches, each with its own story to tell about whose hand \u2014 or paw, or claw \u2014 carried it there. Axes Mundi that lead to nowhere flicker in and out of reality based on portents associated with long-dead pantheons. Powerful telescopes capture photographs of planets in deep space that change appearance periodically according to the tides of mutable creation histories. Intrepid pilgrims comb the World's every corner for hints to tales unspun and not yet spun alike.<br /> <br /> In broad strokes, the history of the World is easily recognizable. All the major wars happened just as our world remembers them. All the geological and geographical shifts are familiar. Electricity still powers technology, Hollywood still produces multi-million dollar films, and people still commute back and forth to work on traffic-clogged roads. It's in the details where the World starts to look more varied and strange. It's in the motivations behind significant events and the heavier hand of Fate in all things. Some events had different outcomes, where the gods' more direct influence shifted a few pieces on the board here and there, and the dominoes fell in different patterns when the dust cleared. Far fewer people in the World believe in mere coincidence, and even randomness has meaning in a universe where Chaos is a demonstrable Purview of divine power.<br /> <br /> With the gods' children wandering the World, it's easy to imagine that every luminary and revolutionary was a Scion. Some of them certainly were. Fate's influence reverberated throughout Europe during the Romantic period as Lord Byron built up and then shattered Fatebound connections one after the other, leading to whole new genres of literature and birthing the modern concept of \u201c celebrity.\u201d Mongolian Scion Khutulun earned ten thousand horses from failed suitors who couldn't win a wrestling match against her and led her warriors in battle with unparalleled ferocity while simultaneously acting as her father's most valuable advisor. Imhotep, chancellor to the pharaoh and son of Ptah, was the World's first in an absurd number of constructive and artisanal fields. Then he built his own tomb and hid it so well that to this day, children of the Netjer seek its buried stones.<br /> <br /> Because all myths are true and the ripples of Fate make them crash into one another on a regular basis, many violent upheavals in the World's history have divine motivations lurking behind their earthly facades. When Scions get involved, the facade is more of a clear glass window, but even then events remain more or less recognizable. These deity-driven wars and invasions more heavily impact Terra Incognita, shifting the balance of power across the Overworld or changing the nature of a god-realm depending on who wins.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, they begin in the Overworld only to spill out into the World through worshipers, and other times a Scion sounds the battlecry first and the gods who would profit from her victory gather behind it. The American occupation of Haiti, for example, had dark overtones of warring against the Loa. The Knights Templar led Crusades in an attempt to wipe out pantheistic worship altogether. Caesar's campaign in Gaul wasn't a dubiously legal quasi-war, it was a one-Scion campaign of annihilation and deification by the self-professed Son of Venus against the Gods of the Sacred Shrines. The Theoi (known by a different name, then) killed most of the Nemetondevos while the Romans enslaved their worshipers, and Caesar finally attained the requisite deeds needed to complete Divus Iulius' apotheosis after mortal death. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T04:33:32-07:00","id":976461,"title":"","content":"The way I have always played it is that while the Gods and Scions are not actively keeping things secret... Fate is arranging things so that no real evidence is left behind to prove that the Gods, Titans or Scions are near.<br /> <br /> \u200bOf course, there will be witnesses to these actions... some times a lot of witnesses... but cameras and other recording devices will mysteriously malfunction or the pictures will be too blurry to make anything out (and no enhancement programs seem to work on cleaning up such pictures). Even the eye witness reports are likely to have wild inaccuracies... or just sound preposterous (especially if there is a more plausible explanation for such an incident). In short... Fate has decreed (for now) that the vast public won't learn the truth (even if a very small percentage gets a glimpse of it). Of course this isn't likely to last forever... for the more people see, the more they believe... and the less hold Fate has on keeping things quiet. With the escape of the Titans, their war with the Gods is growing in scope... and is beginning to spill out into the World where ordinary people can witness it. There will come a time when such belief will reach a tipping point where so many people believe that Fate will no longer keep things hidden. When that will happen or how the truth comes out... no one knows, but even then it is likely that some will still refuse to believe the evidence of their own eyes.<br /> <br /> \u200bThink of it as being similar to the belief in UFOs. When the phenomena first began, the number of witnesses were few, the footage was poor and most were not really believed. Yet as the years passed and the number of witnesses grew... more and more clearer pictures appeared... pictures that are becoming harder to discount. More and more people believe that something is out there... though few agree on just what it is. Meanwhile, attempts by those to prove that these incidents are hoaxes and tricks are accused of covering the truth up (even when it can be proved that something was faked).<br /> <br /> \u200bLike I said... this isn't a perfect cover-up... as those closest to such incidents (and most likely to be fate-bound to those involved) will remember (though maybe not accurately). They have seen past the thin veneer of normalcy to the true nature of the world. They may not have proof of what they have seen, but that doesn't change what they have witnessed. This could lead to worship of Scions as saviors... or to witch hunts out of fear of what happened. Some are likely to search for a way to prove what they have seen... becoming more and more frustrated with each set back. For every positive reaction, there is likely to be a negative one as well. Just because one can't prove the truth (yet) doesn't mean they stop trying... and if they can identify a Scion... well... let's just say that such individuals could be more persistent, annoying and tenacious than even the worst paparazzi could be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":2243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","user":"Shadowstripe","date":". 10-03-2016, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}